<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Carlos Arroyo del Río</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1893">1893</a>–<a href="/years/1969">1969</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Carlos Arroyo del Río was a Liberal lawyer from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guayaquil">Guayaquil</a> who served as president of Ecuador from 1940 to 1944. His government suffered defeat in the war with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a> in 1941 and signed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-protocol">Rio de Janeiro Protocol</a> in 1942, which gave most of the disputed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amazon">Amazon</a> to Peru. He was overthrown by a popular revolt in May 1944, known as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glorious-revolution-spain">La Gloriosa</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/carlos-arroyo-del-rio.jpg" alt="Carlos Arroyo del Río" width="320" height="411" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Marium Alberto · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Carlos_Alberto_Arroyo_del_R%C3%ADo_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
